<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Oriental Republic of Uruguay</h1><p class="st-meta">1828 CE – present · capital Montevideo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The small republic between Argentina and Brazil, created as a buffer state in 1828, which built one of the earliest welfare states in the Americas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/preliminary-peace-convention">Preliminary Peace Convention</a> of 1828, mediated by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a>, ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisplatine-war">Cisplatine War</a> between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata</a> and made the former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisplatina">Cisplatina</a> an independent state. Its first constitution was sworn on 18 July 1830, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fructuoso-rivera">Fructuoso Rivera</a> became the first president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Politics were long dominated by two parties, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-party-uruguay">Blancos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado-party-uruguay">Colorados</a>, whose rivalry led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguayan-civil-war">Guerra Grande</a> of 1839 to 1851, with a nine-year siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a>. Immigration from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and exports of beef and wool brought prosperity. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-batlle-y-ordonez">José Batlle y Ordóñez</a>, president in the early 20th century, introduced social welfare, secular education and the eight-hour day. Political violence involving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tupamaros">Tupamaros</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a> preceded a military dictatorship from 1973 to 1985.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Democracy returned in 1985, and the left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/broad-front-uruguay">Frente Amplio</a> governed from 2005 to 2020 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabare-vazquez">Tabaré Vázquez</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-mujica">José Mujica</a>, legalising cannabis in 2013, and returned to power in 2025 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamandu-orsi">Yamandú Orsi</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> ranks among <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-america">Latin America's</a> most stable democracies.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/oriental-republic-of-uruguay.jpg" alt="Oriental Republic of Uruguay" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: See File history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Uruguay.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1828 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Montevideo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Fructuoso Rivera, José Batlle y Ordóñez, José Mujica</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism, secular</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/uruguay">Uruguay</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uruguay, State of Montevideo, República Oriental del Uruguay</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1927&amp;focus=oriental-republic-of-uruguay" aria-label="Oriental Republic of Uruguay on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3255 3440 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Oriental Republic of Uruguay lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3575 3696L3575 3696M3575 3696L3846 3279"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3575 3696h0M3846 3279h0"/><path class="map-